"""Build the public evidence page from measured discovery artifacts."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re
from site_shell import apply_shell

root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
d=json.loads((root/'docs/data/trump/reference-run.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
f=lambda n:f'{n:,}'
params=d['parameters'];statuses=d['candidate_status_counts']
ordered=sorted(d['topics'],key=lambda t:t['count'],reverse=True)
imbalance=f"The selected solution is highly imbalanced: the largest group contains {f(ordered[0]['count'])} posts, while the remaining groups contain {' and '.join(f(t['count']) for t in ordered[1:])}. Close reading shows a broad dominant group and small event-specific lexical groups. The unweighted mean coherence gives each topic equal weight regardless of its size, so small internally similar groups can raise the score. This result is useful diagnostic evidence, not a finished taxonomy. Before research classification, review corpus coverage, repetition and alternative candidate settings; record any revised selection rule as a new analysis."
topics=''.join(f'<tr><td>Topic {t["id"]}</td><td>{html.escape(", ".join(t["words"][:6]))}</td><td>{f(t["count"])}</td></tr>' for t in d['topics'])
body=f'''<p class="eyebrow">The evidence behind the tutorial</p><h1>Inspect the run.<br>Follow the decisions.</h1><p class="lede">One public corpus. One recorded discovery search. The walkthrough makes the inputs, model outputs and handoff to human interpretation visible.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn primary" href="../app/">Explore the walkthrough →</a><a class="btn" href="../data/trump/reference-evidence.zip">Download the run evidence</a></div>
<div class="tutorial-metrics"><div class="tutorial-metric"><strong>{len(d['topics'])}</strong><span>topics discovered</span></div><div class="tutorial-metric"><strong>{params['coherence']:.4f}</strong><span>selected cᵥ coherence</span></div><div class="tutorial-metric"><strong>{100*d['outliers']/d['discovery_records']:.1f}%</strong><span>modeled posts left as outliers</span></div></div>
<h2>Start with the language. Look beyond the score.</h2><p>Coherence measures association among representative words. Researchers still need to inspect the posts, coverage and domain context. These groups describe the selected Trump account archive; they are not the dissertation’s topics or a human-approved political taxonomy.</p><div class="tutorial-table"><table><caption>Recorded non-outlier topics</caption><thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Representative words</th><th>Posts</th></tr></thead><tbody>{topics}</tbody></table></div>
<h2>Every source post is accounted for.</h2><p>The canonical corpus has <strong>{f(d['source_records'])} posts</strong>, June 16, 2015 through January 8, 2021. Preprocessing leaves {f(d['discovery_records'])} modeled texts. The other {f(d['excluded_empty'])} have no remaining tokens and are retained in the source corpus and exclusion record. Of the modeled texts, {f(d['discovery_records']-d['outliers'])} enter a topic and {f(d['outliers'])} remain outliers.</p><p>The period chart uses all source posts in each period as its denominator. It describes this model’s assignments and coverage. It does not substitute topic membership for validated theme prevalence.</p>
<h2>Know which kind of evidence you are seeing.</h2><div class="tutorial-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>What it establishes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Recorded discovery</td><td>Measured output of the maintained Python search on this public corpus</td></tr><tr><td>Live naming and classification</td><td>New, bounded OpenAI responses for you to inspect</td></tr><tr><td>Your draft theme map</td><td>Your learning exercise, explicitly without formal research approval</td></tr><tr><td>Dissertation and two papers</td><td>Historical research applications, available unchanged in the research library</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Research classification requires actual theme review and an independent benchmark. No completed Trump human review or validated classifier is asserted. Topic models and LLMs include probabilistic steps; changes in seeds, model revisions or dependencies can alter outputs.</p>
<details class="tutorial-note"><summary>Inspect the exact search and artifacts</summary><div class="tutorial-table"><table><tbody><tr><th>Search</th><td>50 parameter draws × ceilings 2–25; seed 42; fit once then reduce</td></tr><tr><th>Candidate status counts</th><td>{html.escape('; '.join(k+': '+f(v) for k,v in statuses.items()))}</td></tr><tr><th>Selected iteration / ceiling</th><td>{params['iteration']} / {params['max_topics']}</td></tr><tr><th>UMAP</th><td>{html.escape(json.dumps(params['umap_params']))}</td></tr><tr><th>HDBSCAN</th><td>{html.escape(json.dumps(params['hdbscan_params']))}</td></tr><tr><th>Model reload</th><td>Saved assignments verified against the reloaded fitted model</td></tr><tr><th>Discovery API calls</th><td>0; computation ran locally</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><a href="../data/trump/reference-run.json">Run summary</a> · <a href="../data/trump/reference/all_iteration_results.json">Every candidate</a> · <a href="../data/trump/reference/assignments.csv">Assignments by ID</a> · <a href="../data/trump/reference/excluded.csv">Exclusions by ID</a> · <a href="../data/trump/reference/run_manifest.json">Environment and model hash</a> · <a href="../data/trump/reference/artifact-integrity.json">Artifact checksums</a></p><p>The fitted model is generated by the local recipe; its hash is recorded. Only load pickle artifacts you trust.</p><figure><img src="../data/trump/reference/coherence_curve.png" alt="Coherence scores across topic ceilings for the selected parameter draw" style="width:100%;height:auto"><figcaption>The selected parameter draw across requested topic ceilings. Actual topic counts can be lower than their ceiling.</figcaption></figure></details>
<h2>Take the next step in your fork.</h2><p>Verify the input, rerun discovery, collect naming evidence and have researchers interpret it. The package records each stage and stops at review and validation gates.</p><div class="evidence-links"><a href="../reproduce/">Fork + run</a><a href="../paper/">Standalone methods</a><a href="../data/README.md">Data card and attribution</a><a href="../audit/">Research in action</a></div>'''
body=body.replace('<h2>Every source post is accounted for.</h2>',f'<h2>Read the imbalance as evidence.</h2><p>{imbalance}</p><h2>Every source post is accounted for.</h2>')
page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Tutorial evidence — TopicLLM</title><meta name="description" content="Inspect the actual Trump corpus discovery run, assignments, exclusions and reproducibility artifacts."><link rel="stylesheet" href="../site.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../reproduce.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../tutorial.css"></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to evidence</a><main id="main" class="reproduce">{body}</main></body></html>'''
(root/'docs/validation/index.html').write_text(apply_shell(page),encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
paper=root/'docs/paper/index.html';text=paper.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
summary=f'''<p id="reference-run-summary">The recorded run selected {len(d['topics'])} non-outlier topics at c<sub>v</sub> = {params['coherence']:.4f} (iteration {params['iteration']}, requested ceiling {params['max_topics']}). It assigned {f(d['discovery_records']-d['outliers'])} modeled posts to topics and left {f(d['outliers'])} as outliers ({100*d['outliers']/d['discovery_records']:.1f}% of modeled texts). Candidate statuses were {html.escape('; '.join(k+': '+f(v) for k,v in statuses.items()))}. The saved fitted model’s assignments were verified after reload. These are measured discovery outcomes, not human-approved themes or classifier validation. The downloadable execution record includes all candidates, assignments, exclusions, environment and hashes. No target topic count was imposed.</p>'''
text=re.sub(r'<p id="reference-run-summary">.*?</p>',lambda _:summary,text,flags=re.S)
text=re.sub(r'<p id="reference-run-interpretation">.*?</p>','',text,flags=re.S)
text=text.replace(summary,summary+f'<p id="reference-run-interpretation">{imbalance}</p>')
paper.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
briefing=root/'docs/guide/knowledge.md';text=briefing.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
measured=f'''<!-- BEGIN MEASURED TUTORIAL -->
## Recorded Trump tutorial execution

The completed reference search evaluated 1,200 candidates over 50 parameter draws. It selected {len(d['topics'])} non-outlier topics with c_v {params['coherence']:.4f}, iteration {params['iteration']}, requested ceiling {params['max_topics']}. Of {f(d['source_records'])} source posts, {f(d['discovery_records'])} were modeled; {f(d['excluded_empty'])} had no tokens after preprocessing. {f(d['discovery_records']-d['outliers'])} modeled posts entered topics and {f(d['outliers'])} remained outliers ({100*d['outliers']/d['discovery_records']:.1f}% of modeled posts). The saved model was reloaded and its assignments verified. Discovery made no paid API calls. This is measured model output, not an approved taxonomy or independently validated classifier. See /validation/ and /data/trump/reference-run.json for the actual record.
{imbalance}
<!-- END MEASURED TUTORIAL -->

'''
text=re.sub(r'<!-- BEGIN MEASURED TUTORIAL -->.*?<!-- END MEASURED TUTORIAL -->\s*','',text,flags=re.S)
text=text.replace('## Original research context',measured+'## Original research context')
briefing.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
print('Built the evidence page, methods result paragraph and guide briefing from the recorded run.')
